<title>HONG KONG: Shougang Tech 1996 net rises 17 percent.</title>
<headline>Shougang Tech 1996 net rises 17 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	6.6    vs  7.2 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents) 1.0    vs  1.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     nil    vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			 35.10  vs  30.07</p>
<p>    Turnover		  697.68 vs  661.68</p>
<p>    Company name	    Shougang Concord Technology Holdings</p>
<p>				  Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close	     June 10-12</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	July 31</p>
<p>NOTE - Shougang Concord Technology is a maker of telephones, power cords and plugs.</p>
<p>The calculation of the share earnings is based on the weighted average of 533.73 million shares vs 415.04 million shares in issue during the year, after adjustment for the rights issue. The comparative share earnings has also been adjusted for the rights issue accordingly.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is two H.K. cents (including interim dividend of one cent) vs one cent.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
